---
// Generated from the live WordPress page, then tidied by hand where needed.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RegularsSignup from '../components/RegularsSignup.astro';
---

<Layout title="Roadmap - clamcentral.com">
	<main class="px-4 pt-12 pb-20" style="background: #ffffff">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-[1038px]">
			<h1 style="font-size:clamp(35px, 3.64vw, 51px);line-height:1.00;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:16px">Development Roadmap</h1>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>Bible Learning Activities Packs • NEW!</strong></h2>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">I have 800+ Bible Learning Activities (BLAs), many should work great with just about any lesson in the Sunday School curriculum you are using right now. Even the best curriculum has some clinkers now and then. These BLAs are curated, categorized, designed to be fun and biblically profound. Lots are available now and many more are arriving soon. The CLAMcentral Regulars Newsletter will keep you updated.</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>PS: The activities are from the CLAMbake lessons, but all references to CLAMbake have been removed.</strong> <strong>These activities really are intended to be used with any Sunday School curriculum!</strong></p>
			<h2 style="font-size:clamp(20px, 2.14vw, 30px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:left;font-weight:700;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:8px"><strong>Migrating the Website in December</strong></h2>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">CLAMcentral is a WordPress site. Running a WP site is time-consuming and fairly expensive. Also, there are many points where things can break. Throughout November I've been switching out of the WP universe to a faster, much less expensive system with many fewer potential problems. The new site will look exactly the same as the old, you won't notice a difference when I "pull the switch" to go live. All clickable links will be the same. The only issue will be for me to choose a new email provider to host my personal CLAMcentral email. That will go down when I make the switch so I'll need to deal with that asap. That's the news!</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em">God's blessings,</p>
			<p style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.64vw, 23px);line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;margin-bottom:1em"><strong>Tom Finley</strong></p>
		</div>
	</main>
	<RegularsSignup heading="Grab my NEWSLETTER!" perks={["Follow the progress of the HUGE <strong>3-Steps to Discipleship</strong> program that rapidly accelerates the success of your ministry.", "Be the first to know about<strong> this and other </strong><strong>new resources</strong> as they arrive.", "The newsletter is sent to your email address <strong>once a month</strong> (more or less predictably!)"]} sectionBg="#ffffff" />
</Layout>
